docs {
  # Inventory Adjustment (Technician Reporting)

  Manual inventory adjustment from `/technician/reporting`. Kalnostics passes these
  through to the inventory app's `/proforma-consumption/adjustment/*` endpoints,
  forwarding the caller's JWT and resolving the order's branch + lab-test source ids
  server-side (the client never supplies a branchId).

  Two scopes, chosen by the tenant's `manualAdjustmentMode` (Inventory Settings):
  - **Order Type** → one adjustment for the whole order (`order-adjustment`).
  - **Test Type** → one adjustment per lab test (`test-adjustment`, keyed on the
    lab report id).

  Each load returns, per product: `plannedQty`, `previouslyDeductedQty`,
  `currentStock`, `finalQtySuggestion`. Each save sets the final deducted quantity
  per product and applies only the DIFFERENCE to stock (idempotent; re-saving the
  same values is a no-op). When automatic reduction is OFF, the first save performs
  the initial deduction. Insufficient stock → 409 `INSUFFICIENT_INVENTORY_STOCK`.

  Set `{{adjOrderId}}` (an `Order.id`) and `{{adjLabReportId}}` (an order
  item's lab report id) to try these. Requires the inventory app running and
  `INVENTORY_API_BASE_URL` set; otherwise loads return an empty view.
}
